#> source: n;d
# 3. Undo double-spacing. Pement: sed 'n;d'
# n prints the current line and reads the next one into its place; d deletes
# that one. So lines 1, 3, 5 ... are printed and 2, 4, 6 ... (the blank ones)
# vanish. It assumes the even lines are the blank ones.
# Try: swap it to  n;n;d  to delete every third line instead.
n;d

